PickLE

An application and a parsing library to create an electronic component
pick list file format designed to be human-readable and completely
usable in its own plain-text form. You can think of it as Markdown for
your project's pick lists.

hMarkdown file syntax	URL:https://daringfireball.net/projects/markdown/syntax

The name of the project is supposed to be a fun little combination of
the words in the phrase [Pick] [L]ist for [E]lectronics.

This project was conceived out of a need to create pick lists for my
company when we were building/assembling projects for customers,
allowing us to quickly create definition files that compiled all the
necessary information about a project's prototype or production run.

hOriginal library and reference implementation	URL:https://github.com/nathanpc/pickle

The first library and reference implementation, was developed in Perl,
as this allowed us to quickly develop the parser for the file, since
it's easily parseable with regular expressions, although ports have
been made for many other languages due to some of our internal
requirements and projects.

